## Modeling a Song

A song has three essential pieces of data: what it's called, who made it, and how long it lasts.

### The Song Struct

```xiom
type Song = {
  title: Str;
  artist: Str;
  duration_sec: Int;
}
```

### Creating Songs

```xiom
let track1 = Song{ title: "Neon Lights"; artist: "Synthwave Kid"; duration_sec: 217; };
let track2 = Song{ title: "Midnight Drive"; artist: "Synthwave Kid"; duration_sec: 194; };
let track3 = Song{ title: "Stargazer"; artist: "Cosmic Beats"; duration_sec: 245; };
```

### Formatting a Song

A method that produces a readable display string:

```xiom
fn Song.format(self) -> Str {
  let mins = duration_sec / 60;
  let secs = duration_sec % 60;
  return "\"" + title + "\" by " + artist + " (" + mins + ":" + secs + ")";
}
```

### Building a Mini Playlist

```xiom
fn playlist_duration(tracks: Song, tracks: Song, tracks: Song) -> Int {
  return tracks.duration_sec + tracks.duration_sec + tracks.duration_sec;
}
```

This gives you all the basics: create songs, display them, and compute totals.

